# Cloudflare Workers static assets redirects. One rule per line: <from> <to> <status>
# Limits: 2,000 static + 100 dynamic rules. Supported codes: 301, 302, 303, 307, 308.
# Rules here run before Cloudflare's own trailing-slash handling.
#
# HOW TO ADD A 301 (permanent) REDIRECT
#   1. <from> is the old path only, no domain: /about-us.html  (not https://example.com/about-us.html)
#   2. <to> is the new page, always ending in a slash: /about/   (or a full https:// URL for another site)
#   3. Status is 301 for pages that moved for good.
#   4. One line per old URL. Run `npm run build`, push, then check with:
#        curl -sI https://<site>/about-us.html   -> expect "301" and "location: /about/"
#
# Wildcards: /blog/* /news/:splat 301 sends every /blog/... URL to the same path under /news/.
# Query strings (?page=2) are ignored when matching.

# --- Old website URLs (replace with the client's real list from a crawl of their old site) ---
/home.html / 301
# /old-about-us.html /about/ 301

# --- Trailing slash: every page URL ends in "/" (see astro.config.mjs and wrangler.jsonc) ---
# Without these lines Cloudflare still adds the slash, but with a temporary 307 redirect.
# Add one line per page so search engines get a permanent 301. Do not add one for "/".
# /about /about/ 301
